Mozambique’s online casino rules take effect on 20 November

Decree 61/2026 sets out the framework for licensed online gambling under the General Inspectorate of Games (IGJ). Operators will need at least MZN100 million in share capital, MZN25 million in guarantees, a .mz domain and in-country data storage for ten years. Players must set daily, weekly and monthly deposit limits at registration. No date has been set for applications to open.

